{
  "dom_id": "step-q73386",
  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14227291/assets/bdce9d030776f147aa7a17881dc5369fc9e7f3a7f4776852d9f5d958ca526baa.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $h(x)$ is shown above. Find the value of $\\frac{b}{a}$ given that:\n\n- $h(x)\\to \\infty $ as $x\\to a$\n\n- $h(x)\\to -\\infty $ as $x\\to b$",
  "worked_solution": "From the given graph, we see that as $x$ approaches $-2$ the values of $h(x)$ increase, approaching $\\infty .$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14227291/assets/02bb73c2c981a0fb9e128b89862b854f9fb6af6cca6ff216a69733561ae90dbf.png)\n\nSo, we can write: $h(x)\\to \\infty $ as $x\\to -2.$ \n\nTherefore, $a=-2.$\n\nFrom the given graph, we see that as $x$ approaches $4$ the values of $h(x)$ decrease, approaching $-\\infty .$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14227291/assets/4ce365f8ce995accf041aca6f1ac6ccc24d0b8e835e0d268c433ff244cfcfb10.png)\n\nSo, we can write: $h(x)\\to -\\infty $ as $x\\to 4.$ \n\nTherefore, $b=4.$\n\nFinally:\n\n$$\n\\frac{b}{a}=\\frac{4}{-2}=-2\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
